  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Thursday)\nIssued at 136 PM MDT Fri Oct 2 2026\n\nDry weather is forecast to continue through early next week as \nridging amplifies over the Intermountain West, keeping dry \neast/northeast flow over New Mexico. A subtle east/west oriented jet \nmax is forecast to increase easterly wind speeds across central NM \nSunday, with gusts of 20 to 30 mph likely along a line extending \nfrom Albuquerque to Gallup. The ridge is forecast to migrate \nwestward towards California on Tuesday as a weak shortwave treks \nsoutheast across The Great Basin and southern Rockies. Models \ncontinue to trend even weaker with this feature so PoPs continue to \ntrend lower. At most, the northern mountains may have a few light \nhours with most areas remaining dry. \n\nTemperatures will continue to trend warmer mid to late week as \nridging only further amplifies over the Four Corners region. This \nwill keep dry and seasonably warm weather around through the end of \nthe week. Long-term guidance is all over the place, although there \nare indications that the ridge will break down, potentially favoring \na more active pattern mid-month.",
